    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Signals is an electronic album by Test Card, released on Home Service Recordings. It presents Lee Nicholson’s project in a restrained, atmospheric mode, blending analog synth textures, subtle beats, and gently unfolding instrumental passages into a cohesive late-night listening experience.\n\nThe record draws from post-rock, ambient, downtempo, and dream-pop influences, with acoustic textures, piano figures, and slow guitar patterns adding warmth to its electronic core. The result is a lush, patient album that values mood and gradual development over dramatic shifts, placing it in the lineage of contemplative, texture-focused independent electronic music.\n\nReleased in a limited cream-vinyl edition, Signals was mastered by Antony Ryan at RedRedPaw and features artwork by Nick Taylor.",
